A new episode is out with
@SGHarlekin
's game! Oh, boy!

@thenerdmansion
Non-commercial games are definitely allowed to be submitted! That’s just a rule we use for games we pluck from the wild so that it’s fair game. The only caveat is that we still want to be hard on submissions cuz that’s what we do.
Was there a specific game you wanted us to check out?

@thenerdmansion
hey, grats to braving it out! I know it’s a lot to deal with as a dev.
Tony is a pretty private dude. But I share everything here with him if you wanted to send a message.

@Starmage
well, we don’t really do longplays, we just play for around an hour. Sometimes longer, sometimes shorter. I also get the impression I should double check if you are okay with our vibe. We tend to be very harsh and that can be a turn off for many dev’s.
If you’re okay with all that, we can give it a shot. Next week is a devlog and then we have another submission and then another dev log, but we could get you in after that.

@RCXGaming
Glad to see someone doing a similar thing! I kinda realized this video would be extra boring not only because it's something unflashy/unexciting, but it's extra thought and effort on a tertiary feature. Not only do a lot of dev's struggle to care about such features, but RM dev's especially since so many don't put extra thought and effort into their primary features!
@wilpuri
You know as much as I warn people about our harshness I really should boast our usefulness. As a dev myself, it is insanely helpful to see an actual recording of someone playing your game and reacting to it. It's just a matter of the dev finding the ability to parse what feedback is and isn't useful, and gain a thick skin. I always point out that we may be tough, but the gaming public is way tougher.

