woootbm said:
I'd be interested in seeing what you did. Did you just comment out a single part or is it more complicated than that? I'd love to do this here and in Yanfly's quest plugin. So many unnecessary clicks for the player!
Click to expand...
There's a lot of things I did to tweak it. These are all edits in YEP_EquipCore:
Spoiler
JavaScript:
this.commandEquip();
    this._commandWindow.active = false;
I put these bits in the create section of Scene_Equip. They both skip the command window (eg. Equip-Optimize-Clear-Finish).
JavaScript:
//    this.addWindow(this._commandWindow);
This is commented out to prevent the game from loading the command window visually and do weird overlap nonsense.
JavaScript:
var wx = 0;
    var wy = this._helpWindow.height;
    var ww = Graphics.boxWidth - wx;
    var wh = this._commandWindow.height;
This has WX set to 0, so it expands the Status Window to not have the box-shaped hole that the command window used to occupy.
JavaScript:
Scene_Equip.prototype.onSlotCancel = function() {
    Yanfly.Equip.Scene_Equip_onSlotCancel.call(this);
    if (this._infoWindow) this._infoWindow.setItem(null);
    this._compareWindow.setTempActor(null);
    this.popScene();
};
this.PopScene(); makes it so the game moves back to the previous screen instead of just bouncing back to the command window that no longer exists.
JavaScript:
Scene_Equip.prototype.onActorChange = function() {
    this.refreshActor();
    this._slotWindow.activate();
};
This makes it so that when you change the window to a different actor via pageup/pagedown, it lands on their equipment slots too instead of the command window.
As for YEP_QuestJournal... i just now looked at it. I don't see why the game has to split up the quests into different command buttons (available / failed / completed / all) instead of just having visual signifiers.
Especially when it also has collapsible menus inside of those categories, like... did Yanfly not realize how cumbersome/redundant this would be in an actual game?
Since it's a custom menu and not like, a modified vanilla equip menu, it might take a lot longer.

